  "validity_notes": [
    "HS256 SYMMETRIC JWT FIX (frozen Change 1): testbed_server.py and testbed_server_v2.py converted from RS256 per-process RSA keypairs to HS256 with ONE shared TESTBED_SECRET. IMPORTANT correction to the frozen spec's premise: run_experiment_distributed.py line 109 was INSIDE SingleServerManager.start(), generating a different secret per node (this is what silently re-broke RSA/RS256 when the same secret was reused). This script generates one SHARED_TESTBED_SECRET and passes it to every child node, so tokens created on node A validate on node B.",
    "JSON SERIALIZATION FIX (frozen Change 2): NumpyEncoder + recursive sanitize (numpy.bool_ -> bool, numpy integer/float -> native, NaN/inf -> None) applied to every json.dump (raw evidence, metrics, result.json, provenance.json).",
